From: marks-jhojan <153632015+marks-jhojan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:31:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] run.py: start the UNDS DualSense companion with the game
 when it is installed

UNDS (adaptive triggers, light bar and haptics for the DualSense) ships
its companion as UNDS/UNDS.exe beside the port. Starting it by hand, or
through a launcher of its own, left out every other way into the game:
the launcher's Play, its desktop and Steam shortcuts (--play). All of
them go through run.py, so the companion starts here:

- `UNDS.exe --env` names the variables it wants (UNDS_EVENTS, ...), or
  exits with 1 when the player turned it off in unds_launcher.ini; they
  never override what the player set (the launcher's Environment field).
- `UNDS.exe --attach <pid> --game <port> --log <user>/last_run.log`
  runs in its own minimized console (the game keeps the focus) or, with
  UNDS_WINDOW=hidden, without a window (it writes its own log, and its
  output stays out of this script's, which the launcher reads), and ends
  by itself when this process does, also across executable switches of
  the collection, which happen inside this process.
- Nothing happens without UNDS/UNDS.exe, with UNDS_AUTO=0, or when
  UNDS_EVENTS was already set by someone else running a companion. An
  "Apply and restart" (a new run.py with this one's environment) starts
  a companion of its own: UNDS_AUTO_STARTED marks the inherited value.

tests/test_run_companion.py covers these cases with stand-ins for the
Windows-only subprocess pieces.

